<article class="shell-article">
  <nav class="shell-breadcrumb"><a href="/hc/en-us">Help Center</a> / Shell &amp; Nature Energy</nav>

  <p>In 2023 Shell agreed to buy the Danish biogas company <strong>Nature Energy</strong> for around 2 billion dollars. With the acquisition, Shell became in one move one of the leading players in renewable natural gas (RNG – Renewable Natural Gas) in Europe.</p>

  <div class="shell-callout">
    <strong>What is Nature Energy?</strong> Nature Energy is Europe's largest producer of biomethane, with in-house expertise in designing, building and operating biogas plants. The company produces green gas from waste from agriculture, industry and households.
  </div>

  <h2>Why is Shell investing in biogas?</h2>
  <p>Biogas is a competitive way to reduce CO₂ emissions in sectors that are hard to electrify – including heavy road transport, shipping, heating and industry. It fits Shell's ambition to offer more low-emission solutions while expanding the customer base for liquefied gas in Europe from fossil LNG toward green <strong>BioLNG</strong>.</p>

  <h2>Strong Danish roots</h2>
  <p>Nature Energy was founded in Denmark and today operates a wide range of plants across the country, along with the associated infrastructure and biomass agreements. Danish expertise and technology are now part of a global energy company – and the foundation for Shell's continued growth in green gas.</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Europe's largest</strong> producer of biomethane</li>
    <li><strong>14+ plants</strong> in operation with associated infrastructure in Denmark</li>
    <li><strong>Circular model</strong>, where the residue becomes natural fertiliser</li>
    <li><strong>Part of Shell</strong> since the 2023 acquisition</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The road ahead</h2>
  <p>Together, Shell and Nature Energy will increase biomethane production and expand the number of plants – in Denmark and the rest of Europe. The goal is to deliver more green energy for transport, industry and homes, and thereby accelerate the green transition.</p>

